repository-code: "https://github.com/sinhaparth5/aparajita-memtable"
abstract: >-
  Aparajita is a C++20 in-memory buffer (MemTableRep) for RocksDB and
  LevelDB-style LSM-tree engines, and a drop-in replacement for RocksDB's
  default concurrent skip list. It packs fifteen 32-bit order-preserving key
  surrogates and a sentinel into one 64-byte cache line and searches them with
  a single branchless vector compare, so that the population count of the
  compare mask is the lower bound directly. Point lookups are 22 to 39 percent
  faster than the skip list and ordered seeks 15 to 29 percent faster, at 1, 4,
  16 and 64 threads.
